course: dictionary
lesson: 10735
title: Uprising: the same event, two stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An uprising is when a large group of people rise up together to fight or protest against the people in charge, such as a government or a ruler. «In 1648 Bohdan Khmelnytsky led a huge uprising and built a Cossack state.» The words huge and led are your clues: this was a big event, and it had a leader. Try swapping in rebellion. It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Uprisings are often sudden and sometimes violent. «The 1911 Revolution began with an uprising in Wuchang» shows that one uprising can start a much bigger change. «Crush an uprising» is another phrase to know: to crush means to stop it by force.
explain: The same uprising can be told in different ways. Supporters may call it a fight for freedom, while rulers may call it a riot. Good readers ask who is telling the story and why. Historians look at both sides and name what happened honestly.
fact: An uprising is a large group of people rising up together against those in power.
fact: An uprising is a kind of rebellion or revolt, often sudden and sometimes violent.
fact: «Sun was abroad, in America, when the uprising began.»
fact: «Crush an uprising» means to stop it by force.
fact: «A popular uprising» means an uprising that many ordinary people take part in.
exercise: «In 1648 Bohdan Khmelnytsky led a huge uprising.» What is an uprising? | A long holiday by the sea | *A large group rising up together against those in power | A quiet party for friends | A school sports day with races
exercise: «Sun was abroad, in America, when the uprising began.» Where was Sun when the uprising began? | *In America | At school | In Wuchang | At home in the palace
exercise: Why might two people describe the same uprising differently? | *Each side sees it from its own point of view | Uprisings are always peaceful, so everyone agrees | One of them cannot read | The uprising never really happened
test: «The 1911 Revolution began with an uprising in Wuchang.» Which word could replace uprising with the same meaning? | Silence | *Rebellion | Holiday | Picnic
test: What does «crush an uprising» mean? | *To stop it by force | To make it bigger | To celebrate it | To write a poem about it
exam: A news report calls the uprising a fight for freedom, but the ruler calls it a riot. What should you remember? | News reports never disagree with each other | Riots and uprisings always mean exactly the same thing | Only the ruler's story is true | *Each side may describe the same event differently, so compare the stories
